# Docker build context for examples/shop and examples/hub (both
# Dockerfiles install the framework from this checkout, so the context
# is the repository root). Everything here is either build output that
# must be rebuilt inside the image or noise that would bust the layer
# cache.
.git
# the tree scripts/install-tree.janet writes: 40 MB of the very same
# packages the image installs for itself, one stage earlier
.void-tree
# delivery bodies the hub's dev store kept, and the letters its dev mail
# transport wrote — one machine's data, never an image's
examples/hub/storage
.github
.omc
**/jpm_tree
**/build
**/*.so
**/*.dylib
**/*.o
**/*.a
**/*.jimage
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-*
**/tmp
**/.tmp-*
bench/results
.DS_Store
